WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.620
The Game of Thrones prequel series, House
of the Dragon, although based on George RR

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:10.160
Martin's Targaryen history book Fire &amp; Blood,
will not feature Targaryens only, but many

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:16.160
other houses and many other legendary figures
from that time period as well, including Tyland

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:21.981
Lannister, who in opinion of many was the
hardest and most loyal guy of them all. This

00:00:21.981 --> 00:00:27.760
guy was literally tortured at one point in
most horrific ways and yet refused to betray

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:33.390
the secrets of his sworn King. If there is
any man that served the Hand of the King role

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:39.910
as good and efficient as Tywin Lannister did
to the Mad King, then it's Tyland Lannister.

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:44.740
Tyland fought for Queen Alicent's son Aegon
II and the Greens, but also served the Blacks

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:50.530
and Rhaenyra's son Aegon III and yet he never
broke an oath and remains one of the most

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:55.860
loyal characters in the histroy of Westeros.
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel

00:00:55.860 --> 00:01:01.920
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president
to air in 2022. Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:07.430
Condal will serve as showrunners and executive
producers. George R. R. Martin will also serve

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:13.280
as executive producer. It’s based on George
RR Martin’s book Fire And Blood volume 1

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:17.690
and on Martin’s yet unfinished Fire And
Blood volume 2 book. “Fire &amp; Blood begins

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:22.500
their tale with the legendary Aegon the Conqueror,
creator of the Iron Throne, and goes on to

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.800
recount the generations of Targaryens who
fought to hold that iconic seat, all the way

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:33.420
up to the civil war that nearly tore their
dynasty apart.” That's Fire And Blood volume

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:39.130
1. The yet unreleased Fire And Blood volume
2 will continue from where part 1 ended, with

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:45.200
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war with

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:50.570
Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:54.970
The key event of the show is also the key
in a history of House Targaryen, the Dance

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:59.810
of the Dragons - the Targaryen civil war,
which divided the entire kingdom and launched

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:06.040
a huge war that was fought from 129 AC to
131 AC. The Dance of the Dragons was the most

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:11.180
devastating war in the history of the Seven
Kingdoms. A war of succession between Aegon

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:18.000
II and his half-sister Rhaenyra over their
father Viserys I's throne. Both of them thought

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:23.360
they belonged on the Iron Throne. When people
started declaring for one of them or the other,

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:28.730
their fight divided the kingdoms in two.
Targaryens fought Targaryens, brothers fought

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:33.770
brothers, dragons fought dragons. By the time
it was over, thousands were dead.

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:38.910
Before the Targaryen civil war started, and
thus in season 1, Ser Tyland Lannister is

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:44.099
a knight from House Lannister. He serves on
the small council at King's Landing, as master

00:02:44.099 --> 00:02:49.440
of ships for King Viserys I Targaryen, but
throughout his life he will also serve as

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:55.040
master of coin for Aegon II Targaryen, and
as the Hand of the King for Aegon III Targaryen.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:03:01.400
He is the younger twin brother of Jason Lannister,
the Lord of Casterly Rock. When the Dance

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:06.590
of the Dragons starts, Tyland is one of the
most prominent enemies of Rhaenyra, but in

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:12.440
his youth, to be more precise, in 112 AC,
Ser Tyland and his older twin, Ser Jason,

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:19.310
vied for the hand of Princess Rhaenyra Targaryen,
but with no success. Eventually, Tyland was

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:24.850
named master of ships by Rhaenyra’s father,
King Viserys I Targaryen. On the night of

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:30.099
the death of King Viserys I Targaryen, Tyland
gathered with the other members of the small

00:03:30.099 --> 00:03:35.620
council in Queen Alicent Hightower's chambers.
There, they discussed the succession until

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:41.000
dawn. During the meeting, Tyland pointed out
that many of the lords who had sworn to defend

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:47.530
the succession of Princess Rhaenyra back in
105 AC were long dead. He remarked that it

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:53.720
had been twenty-four years and that he himself
swore no such oath, as he had been a child

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:59.400
at the time, and sided with Alicent’s son,
Aegon, to make him King rather than have Rhaenyra

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:03.940
as the Queen of the Seven Kingdoms. At the
start of the Dance of the Dragons, Ser Tyland

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:09.990
was named master of coin by Dowager Queen
Alicent Hightower. Upon his appointment, Tyland

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:14.670
acted at once to seize the royal treasury
which proved to be one of the best decisions

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:19.799
the Greens have made during this entire war,
but also a decision that would later be the

00:04:19.799 --> 00:04:25.909
reason of a horrendous torture upon him. The
crown's gold was divided into four parts.

00:04:25.909 --> 00:04:31.009
One part was entrusted to the care of the
Iron Bank of Braavos for safekeeping, another

00:04:31.009 --> 00:04:36.960
sent to Casterly Rock and the third to Oldtown.
The remaining wealth was used by the Greens

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:43.249
for bribes and gifts and hiring sellswords.
When King Aegon got severely wounded in a

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:47.939
dragon fight, and Prince Aemond Targaryen
was the Prince Regent and Protector of the

00:04:47.939 --> 00:04:54.319
Realm, Tyland favored Aemond's suggestion
of bringing battle to Prince Daemon Targaryen

00:04:54.319 --> 00:04:59.800
and fighting the rebellious river lords. This
proved to be the biggest mistake the Greens

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:04.749
could do. By leading an entire army and the
biggest dragon, Vhagar, out of King’s Landing

00:05:04.749 --> 00:05:10.279
to fight Daemon in the Riverlands, Aemond
gave Daemon, Rhaenyra’s husband and the

00:05:10.279 --> 00:05:17.270
most experienced general in Westeros, an opportunity
to avoid Aemond and instead go for the defenseless

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:22.490
King’s Landing and to put his wife Rhaenyra
on the Iron Throne, which he did. When Rhaenyra

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:28.460
took King's Landing in 130 AC, Tyland was
among the members of the court who emerged

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:34.300
from Maegor's Holdfast. Tyland was taken and
given to Rhaenyra's torturers, in hopes that

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:39.650
some of the Crown's treasury could be recovered.
However Tyland Lannister proved to be the

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:45.190
most loyal man in Westeros and refused to
tell where the gold had been sent, despite

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:51.379
being blinded, gelded, and mutilated by torturers.
After yet another fall of King’s Landing

00:05:51.379 --> 00:05:56.090
and after Rhaenyra fled the capital, Ser Tyland
was released by the gutter knights of Ser

00:05:56.090 --> 00:06:02.099
Perkin the Flea, who had seized the Red Keep
to install his squire, Trystane Truefyre,

00:06:02.099 --> 00:06:07.699
as king on the Iron Throne. After the city
was taken back by the greens, Tyland was re-installed

00:06:07.699 --> 00:06:12.870
as master of coin. As the armies of the North,
the Vale and the Riverlands, all loyal to

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:18.139
Queen Rhaenrya were preparing to march on
King's Landing, Tyland suggested sailing to

00:06:18.139 --> 00:06:25.240
Lys or Tyrosh to hire sellsword companies
to fight for Aegon II, but Corlys Velaryon

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:30.710
insisted that Tyland could never return with
the sellswords in time. When King Aegon II

00:06:30.710 --> 00:06:36.159
suggested sending Rhaenyra's son, Prince Aegon
the Younger, to the Wall, or gelding him to

00:06:36.159 --> 00:06:42.009
ensure Rhaenyra's line would end with her
only remaining son, Tyland argued for harsher

00:06:42.009 --> 00:06:48.369
course. He suggested Aegon's execution, insisting
that Aegon would always be a threat to the

00:06:48.369 --> 00:06:54.560
king, as long as he lived. Tyland was later
dispatched across the narrow sea to find sellswords

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:59.240
in Pentos, Tyrosh, and Myr.
Tyland returned to King's Landing from Myr

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:04.409
shortly after King Aegon II Targaryen's death.
He was made the Hand of the King for the very

00:07:04.409 --> 00:07:10.830
same guy he wanted to execute, King Aegon
III Targaryen at the start of his regency.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:16.210
He began wearing a silken hood over his head
on formal occasions, as ladies new to court

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:21.369
were known to faint when seeing his face,
the result of all the torture Rhaenrya’s

00:07:21.369 --> 00:07:26.860
men did to him. His hood, however, gave cause
to whispers among the smallfolk, who considered

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:32.819
him a malign masked sorcerer and began calling
him "the hooded hand". Despite having previously

00:07:32.819 --> 00:07:39.699
served King Aegon II and having argued for
the death of Aegon III before his coronation,

00:07:39.699 --> 00:07:46.699
and despite the fact that Aegon III’s mother
tortured him, Tyland served the new king loyally.

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:52.490
Tyland set out to restore trade to the Seven
Kingdoms, which had collapsed during the war.

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:57.779
He abolished taxes that had been enacted by
Queen Rhaenyra Targaryen and Lord Bartimos

00:07:57.779 --> 00:08:02.960
Celtigar, gave out loans for rebuilding the
holdings which had been destroyed during the

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:08.139
war, and ordered the construction of three
huge fortified granaries throughout the kingdom,

00:08:08.139 --> 00:08:13.809
and had them filled with grain. He also ordered
the repair and restoration of the Dragonpit,

00:08:13.809 --> 00:08:18.229
strengthened the city gates, and announced
funding for the construction of fifty new

00:08:18.229 --> 00:08:24.059
war galleys, although only ten were eventually
commissioned. When war erupted once more in

00:08:24.059 --> 00:08:29.610
the Stepstones, Tyland refused the offers
made by envoys from Pentos, Braavos, and Lorath

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:35.380
to form an alliance against the legendary
pirate, Racallio Ryndoon, insisting to the

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:41.011
regents of Aegon III that it was wiser to
keep out of the wars of the Free Cities. In

00:08:41.011 --> 00:08:47.050
early 133 AC, when it was discovered that
Winter Fever had broken out across the city

00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:51.800
and the realm, Tyland ordered the gates of
the city and the Red Keep closed, to prevent

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:57.810
the disease from spreading. But as the Winter
Fever was nearing its end, Tyland himself

00:08:57.810 --> 00:09:03.110
fell ill. He died after only two days, in
the presence of Septon Eustace and King Aegon

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:07.970
III, who took his hand as Tyland took his
last breath.

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:11.160
Tyland is one of the most important characters
in this story.

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:16.020
By moving three-quarters of the Crown’s
gold from King’s Landing while Aegon II’s

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:20.470
master of coin, Tyland had sown the seeds
of Queen Rhaenyra’s downfall,

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:26.580
a stroke of cunning that would, in the end,
cost him his eyes, ears, and health, and cost

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:32.340
the dragon queen her throne and her very life.
Yet it must be said that he served Rhaenyra’s

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:35.880
son well and faithfully.
Tyland Lannister will definitely be one of

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:40.430
the most interesting characters in the House
of the Dragon. An honorable man who lives

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:46.410
and breaths for the realm. Dutiful as it gets,
Tyland's loyalty is that big that he enters

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:51.540
the war healthy as it gets, but at the end
of the Targaryen civil war, he's blind, broken

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:55.440
eunuch for he never betrayed the side he fought
for.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:59.890
All of this and more, Game of Thrones prequel
show, House of the Dragon, brings in 2022.

00:09:59.890 --> 00:10:04.070
Thank you so much for watching. If you enjoyed
this video please give it a big thumbs up

00:10:04.070 --> 00:10:05.690
and I hope to see you in the next one. Peace!

